  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be completed within three years from the date of this permission.Reason: To accord with the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (5) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved drawings:  GLA.125.PR.SP Received: 16 October 2025,  E 00 Received: 14 October 2025,  GLA.125.PR.101 Received: 09 October 2025.  \r\n\r\nReason:  To accord with the provisions of Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph W.12 (a) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  ",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to the occupation of the self-contained basement floor studio flat hereby permitted, one adequately sized, fully enclosed and secure resident cycle parking unit, designed in accordance with the London Cycle Design Guidelines, shall be installed in the south eastern area of the existing building's rear courtyard (accessed from Ridgeway Drive) located in accordance with the submitted Proposed Site Plan (Ref: GLA.125.PR.SP), be made available for use and be permanently retained as such.  \r\n\r\nReason: In order to support sustainable transport objectives in accordance with Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (2(a)) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  ",
    "Condition : 4 - Prior to the occupation of the self-contained basement floor studio flat hereby permitted and notwithstanding the submitted Proposed Site Plan (Ref: GLA.125.PR.SP), an adequately sized and fully enclosed unit for the storage of the residual waste, food waste and recycled material bins specified by the Council's Recycling and Refuse Guidance:  Guide for Architects and Planners (2022) for a one person studio flat (not located above a shop) shall be installed in the south eastern area of the site's rear courtyard (accessed from Ridgeway Drive), made available for use and be permanently retained as such.  \r\n\r\nWaste bins shall be permitted to be positioned on the public highway for collection during designated collection days only, as advised by the Council's Ward Improvement (Waste) Service, and at no other time.  No waste or waste bins shall otherwise be stored on a public highway at any time.  \r\n\r\nReason:  In order to ensure adequate storage provision and collection arrangements (in the context of the site's access constraints) for waste and recycled materials in accordance with Schedule 2, Part 3, Paragraph MA.2 (2(a)) of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).  "
